  "name": "Write LinkedIn posts from Google Sheets topics and approve them by email with PostWire",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b7225c6e-0f7f-4c4b-a284-6e74544e7ff7",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -643,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 750,
        "content": "## Write LinkedIn posts from a topic list and approve them by email\nKeep a list of topics in Google Sheets. Every weekday PostWire drafts the next one for LinkedIn, Facebook and Bluesky, Gmail asks you to approve, and exactly what you approved is published.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every weekday at 9:00** reads the rows marked ready. **Take the next topic** picks the first one and **Mark the topic as drafting** claims it, so it is never drafted twice.\n2. **Write the drafts** (PostWire) writes a different post for each network from the topic and your notes, in your voice.\n3. **Ask me to approve** emails you the three drafts with two buttons and waits for your answer.\n4. **Post the approved drafts** (PostWire) publishes those exact texts. Skip marks the row as skipped.\n5. **Mark the topic as posted** writes the post links in the row. When a network refuses, **Write the fix in the row** and **Email me the fix** tell you what to fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Create a sheet with the columns topic, notes, status, posted_at, links and note. Write ready in status to queue a topic.\n3. Connect Google Sheets and pick the same sheet in the five Sheets nodes.\n4. Connect Gmail and fill in **Your voice and email**.\n\n### Customize\nChange the hour in the trigger, the voice, or the networks in both PostWire nodes (the free PostWire plan posts to 2 networks per post)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
